# Text Processor CLI Tool

A Python command-line tool that reads a text file, processes its content, and outputs word frequency results to another file.

The project demonstrates:
- CLI usage with argparse
- File I/O handling
- Text preprocessing (cleaning & normalization)
- Logging
- Error handling
- Modular architecture (src layout)
- Packaging with setuptools

---

## 🚀 Features

- Reads input text file
- Cleans text (lowercase, removes punctuation)
- Counts word frequency
- Writes results to output file
- Logs execution steps
- Handles common errors gracefully
- Includes execution time decorator

---

## 📦 Installation

### 1. Create virtual environment
```bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

### 2. Install package
```bash
pip install -e .

### 3. Usage
```bash
text-processor input.txt -o output.txt
